  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Is it true that if G is a finite group with all conjugacy classes of distinct sizes,\nthen G ∼= S3 ?\n   This is true if G is solvable (J. Zhang, J. Algebra, 170 (1994), 608–624); it is also\nknown that F (G) is nontrivial (Z. Arad, M. Muzychuk, A. Oliver, J. Algebra, 280\n(2004), 537–576).                                                                Z. Arad",
